All frame components of V-01's Kinnersley frame depend only on `(r, θ) = (x 1, x 2)`. This file computes the
genuine slice derivatives (`HasDerivAt`, no junk values) of the non-constant components, the commutators
`[e_A, e_B]` for `(A, B) = (l, n), (l, m), (n, m), (m, m̄)` and the lowered commutator coefficients
`cL C A B = g(e_C, [e_A, e_B])` for these pairs (the remaining pairs follow from antisymmetry and the reality
relation `cL_swap`). Everything holds on IV's `domReg` for every real `M, a, Q`.

Notation in statements: `q = qK a x = r + i a cos θ`, `q̄ = qbarK a x`, `√2` is `((Real.sqrt 2 : ℝ) : ℂ)`.
-/

